 To convert the number $12345_6$ from base 6 to base 10, we can use the formula for converting a number from base $b$ to base 10: $N_{10} = d_n \cdot b^n + d_{n-1} \cdot b^{n-1} + \ldots + d_1 \cdot b^1 + d_0 \cdot b^0$, where $d_i$ are the digits of the number in base $b$. For $12345_6$, this becomes: \[
12345_6 = 1 \cdot 6^4 + 2 \cdot 6^3 + 3 \cdot 6^2 + 4 \cdot 6^1 + 5 \cdot 6^0 = 1 \cdot 1296 + 2 \cdot 216 + 3 \cdot 36 + 4 \cdot 6 + 5 \cdot 1 = 1296 + 432 + 108 + 24 + 5 = 1865_{10}
\] <answer> $1865$ </answer>

